WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.308
Metacognition is thinking about thinking, but in practice it is more useful than that short definition sounds.

2
00:00:07.308 --> 00:00:15.905
It is the ability to notice your own understanding, strategies, assumptions, confidence, and errors while you are learning or working.

3
00:00:15.905 --> 00:00:26.221
It helps you ask whether you really understand something, whether your current approach fits the task, and whether your confidence is supported by evidence.

4
00:00:26.221 --> 00:00:32.239
Cognition is the mental work itself: reading, remembering, solving, deciding, writing, comparing, or troubleshooting.

5
00:00:32.239 --> 00:00:36.108
Metacognition is the awareness and regulation of that work.

6
00:00:36.108 --> 00:00:39.547
For example, solving a technical problem is cognition.

7
00:00:39.547 --> 00:00:44.705
Noticing that your first explanation depends on an untested assumption is metacognition.

8
00:00:44.705 --> 00:00:46.855
Writing a report is cognition.

9
00:00:46.855 --> 00:00:53.302
Realizing that the report is clear to you but not to the audience is metacognition.

10
00:00:53.302 --> 00:00:58.031
Metacognition matters because many important mistakes happen before the final answer.

11
00:00:58.031 --> 00:01:01.040
A learner may confuse familiarity with mastery.

12
00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:06.198
An engineer may keep applying the same strategy after evidence stops fitting.

13
00:01:06.198 --> 00:01:11.786
A leader may make a confident decision while missing uncertainty in the assumptions.

14
00:01:11.786 --> 00:01:17.804
A writer may produce fluent text without checking whether the claim is actually supported.

15
00:01:17.804 --> 00:01:20.813
The point is not endless self-analysis.

16
00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:23.393
Metacognition is a practical operating skill.

17
00:01:23.393 --> 00:01:30.700
It gives people a way to pause, check, adjust, and improve while work is still in motion.

18
00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:39.297
In learning, technical work, troubleshooting, leadership, writing, and decision-making, that ability can prevent small misunderstandings from becoming larger errors.
